  "goodToKnow": "Wohnhaft means resident, an official word on forms and in police and court reports: Max Muster, wohnhaft in Leipzig. In speech, you'd say er wohnt in Leipzig. Related: der Wohnsitz (place of residence), and in Germany you must register your address within two weeks of moving at the Bürgeramt (Anmeldung). The -haft suffix also appears in ernsthaft and fabelhaft."
